Production of Chlor-alkali, BREF CAK (@ic-chloralkali: 0, is #reference, #part-of @ic-sources) { r_69QNQ29VT4NA2MXHTVWDNP8T2W
European Commission, Joint Research Centre. Production of Chlor-alkali, BREF CAK. published October 2014; BAT conclusions December 2013. [Official reference and full-text access](https://bureau-industrial-transformation.jrc.ec.europa.eu/reference/production-chlor-alkali-0).

This book follows brine preparation/purification, electrolysis, caustic concentration, chlorine and hydrogen conditioning, associated systems, conversion of older cell plants and site legacy questions.

Read the entire book for the sustained chlor-alkali case, including brine, cells, co-products, product purification, resource/energy accounts and environmental evidence. Compare current primary evidence where a historical route appears. Keep the 2014 report separate from the older archived CAK document.

Identity, stated scope, date and official access were checked on 29 October 2026. This is a dated technical reference, not a claim that every described plant, technology or legal reference is current everywhere. Preserve its attribution, actual reuse notice and third-party exceptions; public access is not described as a blanket CC licence. Full-text or automated inspection limits are distinguished where relevant. No book, figure, industrial data or associated media is bundled. The official 344-file-page PDF and published scope were available; the book date differs from the associated conclusions.

